    "updatedAt": "2026-10-22T01:46:06.895Z",
    "reason": "PR #133734 is a semantics-preserving MIR representation change for index bounds checks: the pre-PR `Len(place)` (with InstSimplify folding `Len([_; N])` to `N`) and the post-PR constant length for arrays / `PtrMetadata` for slices both compute exactly the same length for the same place. The PR itself and the frozen analysis explicitly say not to treat old `Len` as wrong. There is no concrete source-level input on which the old and new bounds-check length computations produce different values; constructing one would require inventing an unrelated unsound mutation/dedup scenario or arbitrary return-value change not present in this PR. Therefore no source-grounded original/transformed pair can be validated as a semantic counterexample.",
    "evidence": [],
    "attempts": 0
  },
  "analysis": {
    "originalLogic": "Before this PR, `Builder::bounds_check` emitted a length temporary via `Rvalue::Len(slice.to_place(self))`, compared `index < len`, and used that operand in the panic message. For array places, `InstSimplify::simplify_len` then rewrote `Rvalue::Len(place)` to a `usize` constant when `place.ty` was `ty::Array(_, len)`, using the comment `/// Transform `Len([_; N])` ==> `N`.` The PR changes MIR building so arrays produce an `Operand::Constant` length directly (plus a `FakeRead(ForIndex, place)`), while slices produce `PtrMetadata` from either `copy _n` for trivially-copy references or a marked `&raw const *_n` reborrow for `&mut` / non-Copy cases. Consequently the InstSimplify `simplify_len` rewrite is deleted, the Validator no longer rejects `PtrMetadata` outside runtime MIR, and GVN is expected to deduplicate repeated `PtrMetadata` length computations on the same slice.",
    "incorrectTransformation": "The historical/pre-PR transformation is: for an index bounds check, emit `_len = Len(place)` followed by `_lt = Lt(index, _len)` and `assert(_lt, \"... len ...\", _len, index)`, relying on InstSimplify to replace `Len([_; N])` with `N` for arrays. This PR replaces that with: for arrays, `FakeRead(ForIndex, place)` plus a constant length operand `N`; for slices, `_len = PtrMetadata(ptr_or_ref)` where `ptr_or_ref` is `copy _n` when legal or `&raw const place` for `&mut`/non-Copy places. The two programs should differ only in whether the bounds-check length is `Len` versus `PtrMetadata`/constant, while preserving the same index, panic message operands, and control flow. Do not treat old `Len` as semantically wrong; the difference is representational and exposes different pass behavior and test expectations.",
    "inputDomain": "MIR indexing expressions in Rust source: fixed-size arrays (`&[i32; 7]`), const-generic arrays (`&[i32; N]`), shared slices (`&[i32]`), mutable slices (`&mut [i32]`), boxed slices (`Box<[T]>`), and custom dynamically-sized types with a slice tail (`struct WithSliceTail(f64, [i32]);`). Relevant variations include `-C opt-level=0` for built MIR, panic=abort and panic=unwind, 32-bit and 64-bit targets, constant versus runtime indices, repeated indexing of the same slice in straight-line code, and promoted constant slices.",
    "passIds": [
      "InstSimplify",
      "Validator",
      "GVN",
      "DataflowConstProp"
    ],
    "summary": "Index bounds checks are moved from `Len(place)` to `PtrMetadata`-based lengths: arrays use a constant length plus a `FakeRead(ForIndex, place)`, while slices use `PtrMetadata(copy _n)` when the reference is trivially copy, otherwise a `&raw const *_n` reborrow marked `IndexBoundsCheckReborrow`. InstSimplify no longer performs `Len([_; N]) -> N`; Validator must allow `PtrMetadata` in pre-runtime MIR while still requiring a reference/raw-pointer operand; GVN can reuse one `PtrMetadata(copy _1)` length for multiple bounds checks on the same slice and can const-fold it for known slices. DataflowConstProp array tests still fold the builder-emitted constant length and now explicitly reject residual `PtrMetadata`, while the old DataflowConstProp `slice_len` test was deleted.",
    "kind": "optimization",
    "trigger": "Any lowered Rust index expression `place[index]` on an array or slice, including `&mut [T]` and DST slice-tail places; repeated indexing of one slice makes the GVN deduplication observable; promoted constant slices make `PtrMetadata` constant-folding observable.",
    "preconditions": [
      "The indexed place type must be `ty::Array` or `ty::Slice`.",
      "An array length must be a known const so the builder can emit it directly.",
      "The `PtrMetadata` operand must be a reference or raw pointer.",
      "For `&mut [T]` or non-trivially-copy places, a raw const reborrow is needed because MIR must pass NLL and cannot simply move the reference.",
      "MIRI retagging must recognize the desugared raw reborrow.",
      "Validator must permit `PtrMetadata` before runtime MIR."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
      "Do not use `PtrMetadata(copy _n)` for `&mut [_]` or other non-Copy references; the PR explicitly restricts the direct-copy shortcut to `Copy` types and otherwise emits `&raw const place`.",
      "Do not omit `FakeRead(ForIndex, place)` for arrays: the comment says it is needed so borrow- and initialization-checking consider the place used for partial array tracking.",
      "Removing Validator's phase restriction must not remove the remaining check that `PtrMetadata` operates on a reference or unsafe pointer.",
      "MIRI must skip retagging for the indexing reborrow, via `IndexBoundsCheckReborrow`.",
      "Tests that expect `Len` or expect InstSimplify to fold array lengths must be updated; the deleted InstSimplify `combine_array_len` test no longer applies.",
